  "scope": "A two-packet Einstein initial-data construction has Newtonian leading binding energy when local physical TT packets are held fixed, with an explicit large-separation error bound. This is a conditional nonlinear self-coupling benchmark: the Einstein constraint and G are supplied. No microscopic gravity phase, dynamical packet force, quantum deformation algebra, universal matter coupling, Standard Model, or TOE is proved."
